Package: rowhammer
Architecture: all
Depends: bash (>= 4.0), ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: ncurses-bin, socat
Description: Tetris-like terminal game written in pure bash
 rowhammer is a Tetris-like game that runs entirely in the terminal and
 is modeled after "The New Tetris" (N64). It offers a classic 10x20
 board, the seven standard pieces with a 7-bag randomizer, gravity
 with a level-based speed curve, line clearing, soft/hard drop, pause
 and restart, plus a start menu with configurable key bindings and
 player name.
 .
 The square system (gold/silver bonus blocks) and the persistent wonders
 building mode are part of the game; since 2.0.0 it also has a
 multiplayer for the local network, in which two to six people play the
 same piece sequence on their own boards and send each other garbage
 rows. That part needs socat, which is why it is recommended - without
 it the singleplayer runs unchanged.
 .
 The name is a pun on hammering rows of blocks; the game is unrelated
 to the hardware attack of the same name.
